00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.650
I'd just finished up a job
to steal a dragon egg.

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:16.490
I was camped out by the Zorata Mines,
one of many dwarven strongholds.

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:18.700
It was then...

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:20.540
...that the red dragon appeared!

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:23.870
There's one thing I'm sure of.

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:28.460
A dragon showing no aggression
nor willingness to take flight...

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:29.800
It must be...

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:33.130
NEW SPECIES

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:31.670
A new species!

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:33.170
A mew discovery!

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:36.680
It is just a cowardly dragon
who cannot fly.

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:39.180
We'll have his hide next time, Albert!

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.220
You got it, boss!

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.770
Well? Have you picked up on his trail?

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:49.820
Our info says it was spotted
up at the Temple of Fall.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:52.150
The Temple of Fall?

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:56.990
He's gotta be in there somewhere!
Time for some dungeon diving!

00:02:56.990 --> 00:03:00.410
Don't know if we need to dive at all.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:03.120
Seems the dragon has already moved on.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.540
What?! That info cost us a pretty penny!

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:10.340
We'll just have to make up for it
by lootin' that temple!

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:11.750
That'll pay for our--

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.260
Don't be ridiculous.

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.550
Stealing is a crime.

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:16.970
I'm meowy sorry.

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:20.890
It's easy for adventurers
to forget about things like the law.

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:24.060
Stealing monster eggs for jobs
is completely different.

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:25.770
This doesn't fare well.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:29.230
He's gone into the Forest of the Dead.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:33.190
What, you scared to go in there, Huey?

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:34.740
Yes.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:38.160
All those stories about ghosts
are just stories, dude!

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:39.910
But what if they're not?!

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:40.740
Arrow.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:41.870
Dagger.

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:45.120
How'm I supposed to fight off ghosts
with these basic weapons?!

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:50.170
I can't make stuff explode, or summon
lightning, or resurrect people!

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:52.420
I'm just a regular ol' guy!

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:55.050
C-Calm down, dude...

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:59.550
It's the middle of the day. We got time
before ghosts come out to play.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:02.850
But ghosts aren't the
only thing I'm scared of.

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:04.180
Well, what else, then?!

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:09.900
Look at this shriveled-up forest...

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:13.070
There's gotta be poison gas or
something making that happen, right?

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:15.610
Y-You've got a point...

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:17.740
Let's just... go around.

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:19.360
You got it, boss.

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:27.830
It's a house.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:29.540
Sure is.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:32.500
We're sure a dragon lives in this house?

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:36.880
Yeah, the map we got from those
old grannies says this is the place!

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:39.130
Lookin' for a dragon?

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:42.760
Well, all right, we can help ya.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:45.720
Couldn't let a cutie like you go wantin'.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:48.730
Breaching client privacy is bad practice.

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:50.560
Let's sneak in, c'mon!

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:51.850
Very well.

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:57.820
C'mon, dude.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:00.200
This situation just feels so wrong.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.320
What?! How?!

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:06.700
If this were the situation,
I'd be down to fight for sure.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:09.290
But what if he's just
sitting in his house?

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:11.830
How am I supposed to handle that?!

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:14.880
I can't just barge into a guy's house
without asking for permission!

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:15.880
You can't?

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:21.380
If it looked a little bit more like
a lair, I might be able to handle it!

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.140
How 'bout we just watch
the place for a bit, huh?

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:24.260
Okay.

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:29.980
So this is the Flame Dragon Lord's lair!

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:32.230
Looks like a plain old house.

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:33.400
Look!

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:35.520
That shiny armor! They're Heroes!

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:38.030
They must be here for the dragon, too.

00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:39.820
Where's the loot at?

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:41.070
Gotta be some around here.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.780
They walked in like they owned the place!

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:45.740
Dammit, they'll beat us
to the punch if we're not...

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:47.030
Huey!

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:49.910
You can see inside from up here!

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:52.290
I see those Heroes from before...

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:00.960
Your Flame Dragon Lord ain't here, buckos.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.970
The Flame Dragon Lord?
Is that the dragon's name?

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:07.300
Our awesome boss
is a bit busy at the moment.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:12.680
Y'see, he's plannin' world domination!

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:14.100
Wh-What?!

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:14.980
When did this happen?!

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:17.360
A shocking new revelation.

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:21.990
The boss can turn a whole kingdom to ash
with one puff of his fire breath.

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:23.490
He's that powerful?!

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:27.370
It's only a matter of time until he's
got the whole world in his claws!

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:31.200
Wh-Whaddo we do?

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:34.710
We shouldn't take his
followers' word at face value.

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:39.340
Still, he doesn't seem to be here,
so let's retreat for the time being.

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:41.880
First, let's get us
some fire-resistant gear!

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:42.760
Heck yeah!

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:44.340
The grind begins.

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:51.180
Terrible beasts? In need of materials?
Place a hunter request with us today!

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:51.220
Guild lady!

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:52.140
Y-Yes?!

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:56.230
Print posters for the Flame Dragon Lord
and send them to every guild in the land!

00:06:56.230 --> 00:07:00.110
Wh-Whatever is the Flame Dragon Lord, sir?

00:07:00.110 --> 00:07:03.570
A beast that threatens to end
the world as we know it!

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:08.990
And so, the legend of the Flame
Dragon Lord was spread across the land.

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:12.830
We'll lie in wait for the Flame
Dragon Lord here and ambush him.

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:15.040
We just gotta surprise 'im!

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:16.170
That we will.

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:20.210
By the way, why're we ambushin' him here?

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:21.960
Oh, I just...

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:22.540
...got a feeling.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:23.760
That's your reason?!

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:25.760
I can't believe I'm travelin'
with a half-assed hunter like--

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:27.800
Look! There he is!

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:37.640
Why're there so many people here?!

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:37.640
Ow, ow...

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:40.400
How was I supposed to know
there'd be bandits here?!

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:44.190
Let's just keep an eye on--

00:07:52.790 --> 00:07:54.870
So <i>this </i>is the Flame
Dragon Lord's dark power!

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:56.790
That's how Huey saw it.

00:07:56.790 --> 00:08:00.420
Wh-What now? We gonna go for it?

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:07.010
No, the Flame Dragon Lord is enraged;
we can't ambush him now.

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:09.130
Our plans may have failed this time,

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:11.180
but we're not through with him yet.

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:15.810
One day, our chance will come,
and on that day, his head will be ours!

00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:18.270
Ain't that right, buddy?

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:23.650
Like you could do
anythin' without me, bud.

00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:25.400
I'm with ya all the way!

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:32.450
QUEST: Hunt the Red Dragon!

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:32.450
FLAME DRAGON LORD

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:32.450
FAILED!

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:35.330
Meanwhile, our Flame Dragon Lord...

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:39.290
D-Don't you think that was
going a little too far?

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:41.130
I only burned them to a crisp, that's all.

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:43.130
Which is definitely going too far!

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:47.710
Savages who demand organs
from people they've only just met

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:49.680
are hardly deserving of mercy.

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:51.970
Well, sure, I get that...

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:54.100
And I did restrain myself.

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:56.140
What part of that was "restrained"?!

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:58.060
Look, there.

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:01.190
Their horses and goods are untouched.

00:09:01.190 --> 00:09:02.480
It's a miracle!

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:08.280
The other party seems
to have given up and left.

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:10.740
I'm glad we didn't have
to fight both at once.

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:13.200
What other party?

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:17.950
If they'd attacked from that angle,
I fear I might have blown off your head.

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:20.500
Are you trying to scare me right now?

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:23.830
I wonder what all this stuff is.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:28.130
It would appear that most of these items
were made by companies outside this area,

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:31.010
so I'd fathom these are stolen goods.

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:34.090
Then we should probably get them
back to their rightful owners!

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:37.180
What is it?

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:39.770
H-H-Holy moly...

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:45.310
This is a human girl... right?

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:47.190
This dragon's a fine father of two!

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:49.490
Stop! And who are you talking to?!

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:06.250
So... what do we do with her?

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:10.090
She was probably... no,
definitely kidnapped, huh?

00:10:10.090 --> 00:10:12.590
From what we see here, I'd say so, yes.

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:15.510
Then let's go into town
and tell the guards to help!

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:18.430
A dragon stole away a human child!

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:18.430
They'd likely mistake you
for the kidnapper.

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:19.680
Yeah, figures.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:23.140
I could use magic to teleport her
and these goods back to town.

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:26.190
That's a great idea!
You're so smart, Dearia!

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:28.230
I'm sure someone will
decide to take her home.

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:28.310
Please adopt me

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:29.820
She's a person, not a cat!

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:28.480
Please adopt me

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:28.600
Please adopt me

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:28.730
Please adopt me

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:28.850
Please adopt me

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:28.980
Please adopt me

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:29.100
Please adopt me

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:29.520
Please adopt me

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:32.900
What if someone kidnaps her again?!

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:36.780
Very well. Let us ask her
for her home address.

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:38.620
H-Hold on a sec.

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:39.660
What's the matter?

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:41.330
I gotta find a place to hide.

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:42.910
Why?

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:45.960
She'd get freaked out if she woke up
and saw a big ol' dragon, right?

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:48.040
Ahh, indeed.

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:52.050
Where am I?

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:06.650
H-Hello! I'm not gonna hurt you...

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:16.360
Who are you?! Where am I?!

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:18.530
Did you kidnap me, you insolent peasants?!

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:20.740
Papa!

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:25.830
I am the esteemed daughter of Edred
Wilhelm Ostern Fran Malloy Roy Karlher...

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:31.590
...von Alvin, Andriana Ellen Croixdeia
Margarethe Emmalyn Narsham Felna...

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:33.300
...Kingdom!

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:34.760
Know your place!

00:11:38.140 --> 00:11:39.050
What?

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:40.970
What an impressive name.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:42.930
You dare mock me?!

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:45.890
Letty here was not the one
who kidnapped you.

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:50.810
The real culprits are most likely
those charred corpses over there.

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:55.780
After defeating them, we happened
to stumble upon you in their stolen goods.

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:56.610
What?!

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:59.490
A-And what do you have
to prove that story is true?!

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:03.790
Well, Letty here is quite
the unique specimen of dragon.

00:12:03.790 --> 00:12:06.620
He's sweet, gentle, and kind...

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:08.500
Aww, shucks...

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:12.800
...weak, cowardly, can't handle
hot foods, and can't even fly.

00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:15.130
He could never kidnap someone.

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:18.180
It's true, but you could've
phrased it a little better!

00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:21.890
Very well. I shall take you at your word.

00:12:21.890 --> 00:12:23.930
Th-Thank you.

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:27.770
Especially considering that
pea-brained visage of his.

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:26.050
Pea-
brained
visage

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:27.350
Pea-
brained
visage

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:31.350
Pea-brained visage

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:29.520
He would seem to be harmless.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:31.480
If you'd like to return home,
I can teleport you there.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:34.730
No, thank you. I've actually
just run away from home.

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:36.280
Wait, what?!

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:39.200
Yes, the going hasn't been easy,
but I have no intent of returning!

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:40.530
Very well.

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:42.070
Hold on a sec!

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:45.540
You're so young! You can't
go running away from home!

00:12:45.540 --> 00:12:47.830
I bet your mom and dad
are really worried about you!

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:48.830
Silence, cretin.

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:50.330
Wha--?!

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:53.340
I hear that an elf's wisdom is
greater than any found in a book.

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:54.880
May I ask for yours?

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:56.210
What would you like to know?

00:12:56.210 --> 00:13:00.220
I need to find a house I can
lay low in for the time being.

00:13:00.220 --> 00:13:03.640
Someplace where I might hide
from those who pursue me.

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:05.680
Do you know of any such place?

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:07.270
I just might.

00:13:07.270 --> 00:13:09.940
Is there anything in particular
you'd desire for your dream home?

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:11.560
Let me think...

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:13.650
What about <i>my </i>house, Dearia?!

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:18.190
Seeing as this is a sudden request,
I suppose only one thing is important.

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:22.160
I'd like a building made entirely
of glass, surrounded by tropical flora.

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:24.200
The second floor needs a slide,

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:26.790
and a sculpture of bathing
goddesses in the center...

00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:29.710
As well as a stage where I can enjoy
dance and music performances.

